    "narrative": "LawDog heads into July 5th with a robust lineup, anchored by the high-ceiling profiles of **Lawrence Butler** (71.26) and **Bryson Stott** (71.23). **Lawrence Butler** draws a prime matchup against P\u00e9rez, benefiting from a 10% park boost and a favorable platoon split that elevates his floor. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** is our premier play for the \"SB scarcity\" initiative; despite a -4% penalty for facing a pitcher who suppresses stolen bases, his 50% success-rate potential against Avila keeps him in elite territory. **Taylor Ward** (71.19) is another critical start, leveraging an 18% boost from facing a soft SP_xERA of 4.75 and a substantial platoon edge against Lodolo, making him a primary target for counting stats tonight.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Drew Gilbert** (50.86), who flirted with a start but ultimately remained sidelined. While **Drew Gilbert** offers excellent utility with a 100% stolen base expectation against Gordon, the efficiency metrics of **Daulton Varsho** (52.12) and **Gavin Sheets** (51.06) edged him out due to more favorable lineup positioning and park factors. We are monitoring **Jeremiah Jackson** (56.20) closely; while he holds a spot, his placement in the 8-hole and the difficult matchup against Lodolo result in a marginal grade that puts his roster spot at risk if we need to conserve game caps later in the week.\n\nRisks remain focused on the top of the order for **Luis Arraez** (65.15) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.69), as both face Gordon and his respectable 3.72 xERA. While the park conditions in that contest provide a 14% lift to their scores, they are essentially hitting against the toughest arm on our docket today. **Cal Raleigh** (63.15) provides high-octane production from the catcher slot, though his score is slightly suppressed by the \"dynamic platoon\" penalty against Yesavage. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** still sidelined on the IL, our offensive output relies on this collective efficiency\u2014managers should check weather reports in the late afternoon to ensure no wind shifts negate the advantage **Gavin Sheets** is currently projected to receive.",
